> where is 1/x defined for x an unsigned byte?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = 1/x
  ucas: domain it
domain of it:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires x != 0  (in 1/x)
  defined at 255 of 256 points
  defined for: 1..255
  undefined e.g. at x=0
  C undefined behaviour at 1 points, e.g. x=0
  over all 256 points of the domain
> where is 1/x defined where x is between 1 and 10?
  ucas: it(x in 1..10) = 1/x
  ucas: domain it
domain of it:
  x: int, 1..10
  requires x != 0  (in 1/x)
  defined at 10 of 10 points
  over all 10 points of the domain
> does x times 2 overflow for a signed byte x?
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x*2
  ucas: wrap it
wrap analysis of it:
  2x   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      exact for: -64..63
  over all 256 points of the domain
> does x times 2 wrap around for a signed byte x?
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x*2
  ucas: wrap it
wrap analysis of it:
  2x   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      exact for: -64..63
  over all 256 points of the domain
> the derivative of x squared with respect to x?
  ucas: it(x) = x^2
  ucas: diff it x
d/dx it = 2x
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> the closed form of the sum of i squared for i from 1 to n?
  ucas: it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)
  ucas: closed it
sum(i, 1, n, i^2)
  = n*(n + 1)*(2n + 1)/6
  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)
  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain
